  "desc": "Every image column owns a stable Rec.709 brightness ordering. Hover bends the row-sampling map toward dark-to-bright vertical streams, while leave reverses to the byte-exact source without cross-fading colors.",
  "seen": "Seen on: generative-art portfolios, experimental fashion, music and digital-culture sites",
  "hint": "hover to sort, move the origin, or lock the ordered frame",
  "rootClass": "d-image-sort-v4",
  "libs": [],
  "prompt": "Build v4 Pixel Sort using photo-embers, the unchanged border SVG and all 25 supplied 8×70px gradient columns at x=0,8,…192 and y=80. Preserve their exact repeating endpoint alphas .2/.4/.6/.3/.5 and supplied amber-brown stops; these original overlays stay in their captured layer order over the live photograph. Native output projects the original sorted pixels only below the exact y=80 horizon, keeping the upper photograph intact. The model keeps the complete original stable per-column Rec.709 luminance map, source row indices, smoothstep blend, focus falloff, .11 progress response and 32ms paint cap. Full retains the same complete model and photo-ocean. Shell actions lock/release sorting and restore source; Home/Left/Up restore, End/Right/Down sort, Space locks and Escape restores. Credit Pawel Czerwinski and Adrien Olichon. Use a 240×168 hero plane with the exact 200×150px image frame at (86,28) in the 372×264 stage: 14px corners, the supplied shadow and unchanged original SVG roots without width/height overrides. Full fields retain their original 368×268px geometry in a readable 400px-wide scroll camera. Prefix classes with rootClass and place controls in the shell. Preserve every original numerical model, typed buffer, image dataset, input rule, interruption and paint cap. Support scaled mouse coordinates, native keys and vertical touch scrolling, independent caller/viewport holds, queued intent and full cleanup. Keep the exact captured first pose until interaction, then use interruptible 150ms opacity feedback into the live model. Reduced motion keeps static feedback and disables ambient loops. Portable exports embed both Geist families, approved 800px photography and every photo credit/licence comment; local full views use their 1600px sources.",
